# P4 · Billing, care follow-up and patient portal · Weeks 17–26 · R4 Clinic Ops
# exit: 1 cash close zero unexplained variance 10 consecutive days · 2 invoice formats reviewed by CA (IN) / tax adviser (AE) · 3 0 abnormal results unacknowledged > 72 h · 4 ≥ 30 % bookings confirmed by patients via portal/WhatsApp
# nfr:  1 money integer minor units; idempotent payment webhooks · 2 portal p95 < 2 s mobile; OTP sign-in · 3 released-result rules (doctor controls what/when)
# pkg:  1 billing setup service (price list import) · 2 owner dashboard walkthrough · 3 patient help pages in three languages
# dep:  1 payment gateway merchant approvals · 2 WhatsApp Business template approval

@epic MDV-P4-E01 | Services, invoicing and documents | P4-01, P4-02 | Country-correct price lists, invoices, receipts, credit notes and legal numbering.
@epic MDV-P4-E02 | Payments, packages, dues and day close | P4-03, P4-04 | Collect money safely, track dues and packages, and close the drawer with zero unexplained variance.
@epic MDV-P4-E03 | Closed-loop results and care | P4-05, P4-06 | Every result and follow-up is owned, reviewed and closed with evidence; a sent message never closes care.
@epic MDV-P4-E04 | Patient portal | P4-07 | Patients book, see released records, manage consent and authorise caregivers (incl. Arabic RTL).
@epic MDV-P4-E05 | WhatsApp, discovery and clinic reports | P4-08, P4-09, P4-10 | Messaging patients in their channel, public profiles and owner reports without overclaiming.
@epic MDV-P4-E06 | R4 readiness and gate | P4-02, P4-03 | External approvals, tax review, training and the R4 exit gate.

=== MDV-P4-001
status: Done
progress:
- [PR #53](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/53): `Money` (long minor units + ISO currency, checked, rates rounded half away from zero) in BuildingBlocks.Domain; new Billing module with DOC_SEQUENCE (`billing.DocSequences`) per tenant, country, doc type, financial year and prefix, incremented by MERGE WITH (HOLDLOCK) inside the issuing transaction; EF filter + RLS; `medvya_billing` role without DELETE
- Country rules: India `INV/25-26/00042` (April–March, max 16 characters), UAE `TI-AD-00042` (continuous series: the design carries no year); amount in words (lakh/crore, million) matches the design examples
- Tests on SQL Server 2022: 110 concurrent issues with 10 failing give exactly 1..100, rollback returns its number, FY rollover per prefix, cross-tenant blocked; no float/decimal in domain types or database columns; mutation-checked (unlocked increment, side-connection increment, RLS off, DELETE grant, rounding, overflow)
- Review fix (branch `fix/MDV-P4-001-P0-017-review`): trigger `TR_DocSequences_OnlyMoveForward` stops the app role's UPDATE from rewinding, skipping or moving a series (it was only denied DELETE); MERGE output goes INTO a table variable; Money operators throw ArgumentNullException on null
- Left: issuing invoices and per-facility prefix configuration (MDV-P4-004), cash rounding (MDV-P4-009/012), adviser review of formats (MDV-P4-031)
title: Money and legal document numbering foundation (minor units, DOC_SEQUENCE per country and financial year)
type: Task
epic: MDV-P4-E01
prd: P4-02
covers: nfr:1
priority: MUST
roles: System
labels: billing, money, numbering
estimate: 2
weeks: 17
depends: MDV-P0-016
confidence: 88 | Rules explicit (minor units; numbering formats shown in receipts design).
sources: PRD v2 P4 NFR 1; design/Medvya Clinician App (receipt numbering RCT/25-26/n, INV/25-26/n, CN/25-26/n; UAE TI-AD/RC-AD/CN-AD); docs/02-design/components-theme-copy.md (DOC_SEQUENCE)
desc:
Money value object (bigint minor units + ISO currency), rounding rules per currency, amount-in-words (Indian lakh/thousand; AED). DOC_SEQUENCE per tenant, country, doc type (receipt, invoice, credit, advance), financial year (India Apr–Mar) and prefix, incremented gaplessly inside the issuing transaction.
ac:
- No floating-point money anywhere in domain/database (architecture test on property types).
- Concurrent issuing of 100 invoices produces 100 consecutive numbers with no gaps or duplicates (test).
- Financial-year rollover starts a new sequence per configured prefix.
- Amount in words matches the design examples for INR and AED.

=== MDV-P4-002
title: Services and fees catalogue with price versions, India GST/SAC, UAE CPT/VAT, payer price lists and packages (F-11)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E01
prd: P4-01
screens: F-11
priority: MUST
roles: Practice admin
labels: services, pricing, tax
estimate: 3
weeks: 17-18
depends: MDV-P4-001
confidence: 72 | Price-version rule and preview are designed; settings data truncated; tax treatment must be confirmed by advisers.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (Settings → Services); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#practice-settings-f-08--f-12--medvya-clinician-app--data-truncated-labels-only
desc:
SERVICE_CATALOGUE (name, category, code, SAC (IN) or CPT (AE), tax code, duration) with PRICE_VERSION (amount, currency, effective_from, optional payer price list), packages (items, sessions, validity, price). Editor with invoice line preview; saving creates a new price version effective from a date; archive instead of delete. Note "Tax treatment must be confirmed with your tax advisor".
ac:
- Saving a price creates a new version; issued invoices keep the price version they were issued with (test).
- India services carry SAC and GST rate/exemption; UAE services carry CPT and VAT rate (5 % or zero-rated) per line.
- Payer-specific price lists override the default for insured patients (UAE).
- Packages define sessions and validity and are sellable from billing.
- Changes are audited; only admins can edit.

