=== MDV-P4-014
title: Results intake and inbound report identity match (manual upload/entry; low-confidence needs a human) (C-05)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E03
prd: P4-05
screens: C-05
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Care coordinator, Receptionist
labels: results, matching, safety
estimate: 3
weeks: 19-20
depends: MDV-P2-006, MDV-P2-018
confidence: 82 | Designed; HL7 lab feeds arrive only in P7, so P4 intake is upload/manual entry.
sources: design/Medvya Clinical Screens (C-05); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#care-p4--medvya-clinician-app-medvya-clinical-screens
desc:
Results arrive as uploaded PDFs/images (lab email/WhatsApp from patient) or manual entry of structured values. Matching suggests patients by name, DOB, MRN and open orders; low-confidence matches ("name matches, DOB differs") require a human to choose a candidate or reject. Confirmed results become INBOX_ITEMs linked to the order (state Result received).
ac:
- A result with low-confidence match cannot enter any patient chart until a user confirms (UI + API).
- Candidates show MRN, DOB and open orders; the confirmation records actor and time.
- Matching a result to an open order moves the order's loop state to Result received.
- Unmatched documents stay in an "Unmatched" queue with count.

=== MDV-P4-015
title: Clinical results inbox: severity in words, review/acknowledge, assign follow-up, release to patient (C-01)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E03
prd: P4-05
screens: C-01
covers: nfr:3, exit:3
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: results, inbox, safety
estimate: 3
weeks: 20-21
depends: MDV-P4-014
confidence: 82 | Interactive hi-fi exists but Foundations marks C-01 status "next" (confirm final design before build).
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (C-01); PRD v2 finding CHECK (C-01 "next")
desc:
/inbox: rows with severity (Critical/Abnormal/Normal, icon + word), patient, test, time, loop state (Received · not reviewed → Reviewed → Assigned → Released → Completed). Detail: analyte, value, range, flag, previous value, source and match basis; optional AI context note (dashed, not reviewed). "Mark as reviewed" stores actor/time (REVIEW_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT); Assign follow-up and Release to patient unlock only after review; release follows release rules (doctor controls what/when).
ac:
- Assign and Release are impossible before review (server-enforced).
- Critical results unreviewed after a configurable time escalate (notification to the doctor and covering clinician).
- A patient never sees a result before the doctor releases it (portal test; NFR 3).
- Pilot report shows 0 abnormal results unacknowledged > 72 h (exit gate 3) or lists breaches with actions.
notes:
- Confirm final C-01 design before build (PRD v2 finding).

=== MDV-P4-016
title: Care plans and tasks with owners, due dates, stage tracks and evidence to close (C-02)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E03
prd: P4-05
screens: C-02
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Care coordinator
labels: care, tasks
estimate: 3
weeks: 21-22
depends: MDV-P4-015, MDV-P2-012
confidence: 82 | Designed with stage tracks and evidence rule; "next" status in Foundations.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (C-02 care plans); docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md#care-task-lifecycle-p4
desc:
CARE_PLAN created from a signed note (proposed actions → physician approved): actions (labs, referral, results review visit, adherence call, eye exam) each with owner, due date, stage track (e.g. Ordered → Sample collected → Result received → Reviewed by doctor) and evidence required to complete a stage (e.g. "LR-2311 reviewed", "Call log 11 Oct, 3 min"). Overdue shown in words.
ac:
- Tasks follow the care-task lifecycle; BLOCKED/OVERDUE/CANCELLED/UNREACHABLE require reason and actor.
- A sent reminder or delivered message never completes a stage or closes a task (test).
- Completing the final stage requires evidence (linked record or log entry).
- Owners see their tasks in "My tasks"; reassignment is audited.

