sources: PRD v2 P4 NFR 3; design/Medvya Patient Portal (header text)
desc:
RELEASE records per item (visit summary, prescription, result, document) with who released and when; tenant defaults per type (e.g. normal results auto-release after review vs manual), never auto-release abnormal results without review. Unrelease (hide) with reason.
ac:
- Nothing is visible in the portal without a release record; abnormal results cannot be auto-released.
- Release/unrelease is audited and reflected in the portal within 1 minute.
- Default policies are configurable and documented, reviewed by the clinical advisor.

=== MDV-P4-023
title: Portal booking and reschedule with fee and cancellation policy shown (R-02)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E04
prd: P4-07
screens: R-02
covers: exit:4
priority: MUST
roles: Patient
labels: portal, booking
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 22-23
depends: MDV-P4-020, MDV-P1-022
confidence: 88 | Interactive hi-fi frame with exact rules.
sources: design/Medvya Patient Portal (Book or reschedule); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md
desc:
Visit type (In clinic / Video placeholder until P8), doctor, day strip, available slots (unavailable struck through), optional reason (never shown to reception beyond category), fee and cancellation policy before confirm, confirm → "Booked · confirmation sent"; reschedule/cancel within policy. Uses the same booking path (holds, no double booking).
ac:
- Portal bookings go through the same concurrency-safe booking service (100-parallel test includes portal channel).
- Fee and cancellation policy are shown before confirming; late cancellations follow the policy.
- Free-text reason is stored encrypted and shown only to clinicians.
- Booking source is recorded (portal) for the ≥ 30 % patient-confirmed metric (exit gate 4).

=== MDV-P4-024
title: Portal consent and privacy controls with policy version and change log (R-03)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E04
prd: P4-07
screens: R-03
priority: MUST
roles: Patient
labels: portal, consent
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 23
depends: MDV-P4-020, MDV-P1-019
confidence: 88 | Interactive hi-fi with separate switches and footer.
sources: design/Medvya Patient Portal (Privacy & consent)
desc:
Separate switches: record my consultations (asked again each visit), reminders on WhatsApp (no medical details), share records with ABHA/HIE, caregiver access, health tips & offers; each change creates a consent receipt; footer "Policy v… · {country law} · last change {time}". Withdrawal of recording consent offers audio deletion request (P5-12/H-10).
ac:
- Each toggle creates a new receipt; history is visible to the patient.
- Turning off WhatsApp reminders stops future WhatsApp messages immediately.
- Withdrawing recording preference is reflected at the next visit's consent step (still asked per visit).

=== MDV-P4-025
title: Caregiver proxy authorisation with scopes, expiry, OTP verification and revocation (R-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E04
prd: P4-07
screens: R-04
priority: MUST
roles: Patient, Caregiver
labels: portal, proxy
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 23-24
depends: MDV-P4-020
confidence: 82 | Designed; minor/guardian rules per country need legal confirmation.
sources: design/Medvya Patient Portal (Add a caregiver); design/Medvya Wireframes (R-04)
desc:
Patient adds a caregiver (name, mobile) with scopes (appointments, medicines, lab results, messages) and expiry; invite "they must verify with OTP"; caregiver sees "Viewing as caregiver for {name}" and only scoped items; patient can revoke anytime. Guardian proxies for minors follow country rules (from registration guardian).
ac:
- A caregiver can access only the granted scopes until expiry (authorisation tests per scope).
- Revocation takes effect within 1 minute.
- Caregiver banner is always visible; actions are audited as the caregiver acting for the patient.
- Minor/guardian proxy rules are configured per country after legal confirmation.

