confidence: 55 | DESIGN NEEDED: no screen exists; scope comes only from the October plan line item.
sources: PRD v2 P4-08 (N-02 DESIGN NEEDED); docs/01-prd/traceability.md
desc:
Design first (spike), then Razor public pages per doctor/clinic: name, specialty, qualifications, languages, location, hours, fees (if the clinic opts in), next available slots (live, no PHI) and "Book" into the portal flow; schema.org markup and sitemap. Opt-in per doctor/clinic.
ac:
- A design for N-02 is produced and approved before implementation.
- Profiles are opt-in and show no patient data; availability shows slot times only.
- Pages are indexable (sitemap, schema.org Physician/MedicalClinic) and fast (Lighthouse ≥ 90).
- Booking from a profile leads into portal sign-in/booking.

=== MDV-P4-028
title: WhatsApp reminders and confirmations (EN/AR/HI), opt-in records, delivery status, one-tap reschedule, "doctor running late" broadcast (N-03, design needed)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P4-E05
prd: P4-09
screens: N-03
covers: dep:2, exit:4
priority: MUST
roles: Patient, Receptionist, Practice admin
labels: whatsapp, notifications, design-needed
estimate: 3
weeks: 21-23
depends: MDV-P1-032, MDV-P4-023
confidence: 62 | DESIGN NEEDED for the admin screen; WhatsApp template approval is an external dependency.
sources: PRD v2 P4-09 (N-03); design/Medvya Gap Analysis (WhatsApp reminders SHOULD); docs/03-architecture/integrations.md
desc:
WhatsApp Business adapter in Notifications: approved templates in English, Arabic and Hindi (confirmation, reminder, reschedule link, running late, balance due, portal update), opt-in records per patient/channel, delivery/read status, one-tap reschedule link into the portal, "doctor running 20 min late" broadcast to today's affected patients. Admin screen for templates/opt-ins/status (design first).
ac:
- Only approved templates are sent; messages carry no clinical details (validation).
- Messages are sent only with a WhatsApp opt-in receipt; opt-out via reply is honoured.
- Delivery status updates the notification record; failures fall back to SMS if configured.
- Running-late broadcast reaches only patients booked with that doctor today and is audited.
- Patient confirmations via WhatsApp count toward the ≥ 30 % metric (exit gate 4).

=== MDV-P4-029
title: Spike: reporting store that keeps PHI out of analytics (read replica vs warehouse)
type: Spike
epic: MDV-P4-E05
prd: P4-10
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: analytics, privacy, spike
estimate: 1
weeks: 22
depends: MDV-P0-016
confidence: 75 | Open item in PRD completeness check with a clear decision deadline.
sources: PRD v2 completeness "Reporting store that keeps PHI out of analytics" (decide before P4-10); docs/01-prd/source-conflicts.md (Q-06)
desc:
Decide between Azure SQL read replica with masked/aggregated views and a separate de-identified warehouse; define the metric model for reports and how drill-down to authorised detail works.
ac:
- ADR-008 records the choice, cost and PHI controls.
- Report queries never run against tables with unmasked PHI for non-clinical roles.

=== MDV-P4-030
title: Clinic reports and owner dashboard: appointments, no-shows, revenue, follow-up completion, note time saved (H-07)
type: Story
